interactive (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:49:02.6121789Z Note: a multi-user installation is possible. See https://nix.dev/manual/nix/stable/installation/installing-binary.html#multi-user-installation
interactive (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:49:02.6129828Z ^[[1;31mSwitching to the Multi-user Installer^[[0m
interactive (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:49:02.6220181Z ^[[32mWelcome to the Multi-User Nix Installation
interactive (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:49:02.6229525Z ^[[0m
interactive (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:49:02.6230313Z This installation tool will set up your computer with the Nix package
interactive (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:49:02.6230908Z manager. This will happen in a few stages:
interactive (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:49:02.6231232Z 
interactive (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:49:02.6231473Z 1. Make sure your computer doesn't already have Nix. If it does, I
interactive (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:49:02.6232249Z    will show you instructions on how to clean up your old install.
interactive (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:49:02.6232666Z 
interactive (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:49:02.6232925Z 2. Show you what I am going to install and where. Then I will ask
interactive (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:49:02.6233947Z    if you are ready to continue.
interactive (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:49:02.6234298Z 
interactive (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:49:02.6235015Z 3. Create the system users ^[[34m(uids [30001..30008])^[[0m and groups ^[[34m(gid 30000)^[[0m
interactive (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:49:02.6235706Z    that the Nix daemon uses to run builds. To create system users
interactive (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:49:02.6236732Z    in a different range, exit and run this tool again with
interactive (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:49:02.6237240Z    NIX_FIRST_BUILD_UID set.
interactive (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:49:02.6237515Z 
interactive (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:49:02.6237782Z 4. Perform the basic installation of the Nix files daemon.
interactive (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:49:02.6238196Z 
interactive (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:49:02.6238461Z 5. Configure your shell to import special Nix Profile files, so you
interactive (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:49:02.6238972Z    can use Nix.
interactive (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:49:02.6239234Z 
interactive (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:49:02.6239465Z 6. Start the Nix daemon.
interactive (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:49:02.6239726Z 
interactive (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:49:02.6240312Z ^[[32m^[[4;32mWould you like to see a more detailed list of what I will do?
interactive (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:49:02.6241181Z ^[[0mNo TTY, assuming you would say yes :)
interactive (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:49:02.6241534Z 
interactive (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:49:02.6241697Z I will:
interactive (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:49:02.6242038Z 
interactive (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:49:02.6242304Z  - make sure your computer doesn't already have Nix files
interactive (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:49:02.6242937Z    (if it does, I will tell you how to clean them up.)
interactive (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:49:02.6243508Z  - create local users (see the list above for the users I'll make)
interactive (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:49:02.6244069Z  - create a local group (nixbld)
interactive (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:49:02.6244535Z  - install Nix in /nix
interactive (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:49:02.6245311Z  - create a configuration file in /etc/nix
interactive (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:49:02.6245952Z  - set up the "default profile" by creating some Nix-related files in
interactive (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:49:02.6246505Z    /root
interactive (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:49:02.6254622Z  - back up /etc/bash.bashrc to /etc/bash.bashrc.backup-before-nix
interactive (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:49:02.6255746Z  - update /etc/bash.bashrc to include some Nix configuration
interactive (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:49:02.6264630Z  - load and start a service (at /etc/systemd/system/nix-daemon.service
interactive (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:49:02.6265578Z    and /etc/systemd/system/nix-daemon.socket) for nix-daemon
interactive (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:49:02.6265987Z 
interactive (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:49:02.6266321Z ^[[32m^[[4;32mReady to continue?
interactive (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:49:02.6266829Z ^[[0mNo TTY, assuming you would say yes :)
interactive (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:49:02.6283500Z 
interactive (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:49:02.6284647Z ^[[34m---- let's talk about sudo -----------------------------------------------------
interactive (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:49:02.6293558Z ^[[0mThis script is going to call sudo a lot. Normally, it would show you
interactive (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:49:02.6294529Z exactly what commands it is running and why. However, the script is
interactive (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:49:02.6295337Z run in a headless fashion, like this:
interactive (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:49:02.6295633Z 
interactive (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:49:02.6295880Z   $ curl -L https://nixos.org/nix/install | sh
interactive (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:49:02.6296274Z 
interactive (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:49:02.6296601Z or maybe in a CI pipeline. Because of that, I'm going to skip the
interactive (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:49:02.6297143Z verbose output in the interest of brevity.
interactive (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:49:02.6297434Z 
interactive (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:49:02.6297652Z If you would like to
interactive (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:49:02.6298117Z see the output, try like this:
interactive (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:49:02.6298377Z 
interactive (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:49:02.6298640Z   $ curl -L -o install-nix https://nixos.org/nix/install
interactive (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:49:02.6299219Z   $ sh ./install-nix
interactive (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:49:02.6299425Z 
interactive (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:49:02.6299504Z 
interactive (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:49:02.6299864Z ^[[32m~~> Checking for artifacts of previous installs
interactive (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:49:02.6304320Z ^[[0mBefore I try to install, I'll check for signs Nix already is or has
interactive (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:49:02.6305490Z been installed on this system.
