check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:48:34.4573291Z Note: a multi-user installation is possible. See https://nix.dev/manual/nix/stable/installation/installing-binary.html#multi-user-installation
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:48:34.4581773Z ^[[1;31mSwitching to the Multi-user Installer^[[0m
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:48:34.4671187Z ^[[32mWelcome to the Multi-User Nix Installation
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:48:34.4679453Z ^[[0m
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:48:34.4681055Z This installation tool will set up your computer with the Nix package
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:48:34.4681874Z manager. This will happen in a few stages:
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:48:34.4682236Z 
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:48:34.4682470Z 1. Make sure your computer doesn't already have Nix. If it does, I
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:48:34.4683099Z    will show you instructions on how to clean up your old install.
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:48:34.4683593Z 
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:48:34.4683868Z 2. Show you what I am going to install and where. Then I will ask
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:48:34.4684762Z    if you are ready to continue.
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:48:34.4685086Z 
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:48:34.4685743Z 3. Create the system users ^[[34m(uids [30001..30008])^[[0m and groups ^[[34m(gid 30000)^[[0m
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:48:34.4686407Z    that the Nix daemon uses to run builds. To create system users
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:48:34.4687315Z    in a different range, exit and run this tool again with
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:48:34.4687861Z    NIX_FIRST_BUILD_UID set.
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:48:34.4688170Z 
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:48:34.4688438Z 4. Perform the basic installation of the Nix files daemon.
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:48:34.4688826Z 
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:48:34.4689152Z 5. Configure your shell to import special Nix Profile files, so you
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:48:34.4689649Z    can use Nix.
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:48:34.4690227Z 
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:48:34.4690476Z 6. Start the Nix daemon.
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:48:34.4690690Z 
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:48:34.4691342Z ^[[32m^[[4;32mWould you like to see a more detailed list of what I will do?
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:48:34.4691968Z ^[[0mNo TTY, assuming you would say yes :)
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:48:34.4692316Z 
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:48:34.4692546Z I will:
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:48:34.4693006Z 
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:48:34.4693296Z  - make sure your computer doesn't already have Nix files
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:48:34.4693830Z    (if it does, I will tell you how to clean them up.)
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:48:34.4694431Z  - create local users (see the list above for the users I'll make)
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:48:34.4694962Z  - create a local group (nixbld)
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:48:34.4695438Z  - install Nix in /nix
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:48:34.4695829Z  - create a configuration file in /etc/nix
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:48:34.4696373Z  - set up the "default profile" by creating some Nix-related files in
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:48:34.4696944Z    /root
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:48:34.4706436Z  - back up /etc/bash.bashrc to /etc/bash.bashrc.backup-before-nix
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:48:34.4707999Z  - update /etc/bash.bashrc to include some Nix configuration
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:48:34.4715901Z  - load and start a service (at /etc/systemd/system/nix-daemon.service
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:48:34.4716604Z    and /etc/systemd/system/nix-daemon.socket) for nix-daemon
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:48:34.4717085Z 
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:48:34.4717595Z ^[[32m^[[4;32mReady to continue?
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:48:34.4718174Z ^[[0mNo TTY, assuming you would say yes :)
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:48:34.4735187Z 
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:48:34.4736480Z ^[[34m---- let's talk about sudo -----------------------------------------------------
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:48:34.4745196Z ^[[0mThis script is going to call sudo a lot. Normally, it would show you
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:48:34.4745890Z exactly what commands it is running and why. However, the script is
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:48:34.4746553Z run in a headless fashion, like this:
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:48:34.4746925Z 
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:48:34.4747140Z   $ curl -L https://nixos.org/nix/install | sh
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:48:34.4747446Z 
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:48:34.4747671Z or maybe in a CI pipeline. Because of that, I'm going to skip the
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:48:34.4748373Z verbose output in the interest of brevity.
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:48:34.4748633Z 
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:48:34.4748806Z If you would like to
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:48:34.4749371Z see the output, try like this:
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:48:34.4749607Z 
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:48:34.4750339Z   $ curl -L -o install-nix https://nixos.org/nix/install
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:48:34.4750852Z   $ sh ./install-nix
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:48:34.4751229Z 
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:48:34.4751244Z 
