conformance-update (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:49:06.6827671Z Note: a multi-user installation is possible. See https://nix.dev/manual/nix/stable/installation/installing-binary.html#multi-user-installation
conformance-update (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:49:06.6835914Z ^[[1;31mSwitching to the Multi-user Installer^[[0m
conformance-update (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:49:06.6926446Z ^[[32mWelcome to the Multi-User Nix Installation
conformance-update (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:49:06.6935708Z ^[[0m
conformance-update (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:49:06.6936368Z This installation tool will set up your computer with the Nix package
conformance-update (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:49:06.6937094Z manager. This will happen in a few stages:
conformance-update (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:49:06.6937530Z 
conformance-update (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:49:06.6938032Z 1. Make sure your computer doesn't already have Nix. If it does, I
conformance-update (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:49:06.6938626Z    will show you instructions on how to clean up your old install.
conformance-update (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:49:06.6938952Z 
conformance-update (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:49:06.6940424Z 2. Show you what I am going to install and where. Then I will ask
conformance-update (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:49:06.6941571Z    if you are ready to continue.
conformance-update (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:49:06.6942058Z 
conformance-update (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:49:06.6942603Z 3. Create the system users ^[[34m(uids [30001..30008])^[[0m and groups ^[[34m(gid 30000)^[[0m
conformance-update (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:49:06.6943233Z    that the Nix daemon uses to run builds. To create system users
conformance-update (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:49:06.6944123Z    in a different range, exit and run this tool again with
conformance-update (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:49:06.6944755Z    NIX_FIRST_BUILD_UID set.
conformance-update (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:49:06.6945046Z 
conformance-update (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:49:06.6945479Z 4. Perform the basic installation of the Nix files daemon.
conformance-update (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:49:06.6945801Z 
conformance-update (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:49:06.6946208Z 5. Configure your shell to import special Nix Profile files, so you
conformance-update (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:49:06.6946683Z    can use Nix.
conformance-update (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:49:06.6946894Z 
conformance-update (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:49:06.6947057Z 6. Start the Nix daemon.
conformance-update (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:49:06.6947402Z 
conformance-update (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:49:06.6947990Z ^[[32m^[[4;32mWould you like to see a more detailed list of what I will do?
conformance-update (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:49:06.6948658Z ^[[0mNo TTY, assuming you would say yes :)
conformance-update (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:49:06.6949829Z 
conformance-update (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:49:06.6954163Z I will:
conformance-update (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:49:06.6954555Z 
conformance-update (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:49:06.6954838Z  - make sure your computer doesn't already have Nix files
conformance-update (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:49:06.6955388Z    (if it does, I will tell you how to clean them up.)
conformance-update (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:49:06.6956186Z  - create local users (see the list above for the users I'll make)
conformance-update (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:49:06.6956812Z  - create a local group (nixbld)
conformance-update (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:49:06.6957259Z  - install Nix in /nix
conformance-update (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:49:06.6957682Z  - create a configuration file in /etc/nix
conformance-update (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:49:06.6958342Z  - set up the "default profile" by creating some Nix-related files in
conformance-update (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:49:06.6959445Z    /root
conformance-update (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:49:06.6960501Z  - back up /etc/bash.bashrc to /etc/bash.bashrc.backup-before-nix
conformance-update (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:49:06.6964121Z  - update /etc/bash.bashrc to include some Nix configuration
conformance-update (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:49:06.6974297Z  - load and start a service (at /etc/systemd/system/nix-daemon.service
conformance-update (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:49:06.6975200Z    and /etc/systemd/system/nix-daemon.socket) for nix-daemon
conformance-update (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:49:06.6975511Z 
conformance-update (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:49:06.6976685Z ^[[32m^[[4;32mReady to continue?
conformance-update (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:49:06.6977271Z ^[[0mNo TTY, assuming you would say yes :)
conformance-update (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:49:06.6990414Z 
conformance-update (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:49:06.6991475Z ^[[34m---- let's talk about sudo -----------------------------------------------------
conformance-update (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:49:06.7000062Z ^[[0mThis script is going to call sudo a lot. Normally, it would show you
conformance-update (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:49:06.7000726Z exactly what commands it is running and why. However, the script is
conformance-update (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:49:06.7001439Z run in a headless fashion, like this:
conformance-update (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:49:06.7001720Z 
conformance-update (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:49:06.7002010Z   $ curl -L https://nixos.org/nix/install | sh
conformance-update (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:49:06.7002304Z 
conformance-update (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:49:06.7002621Z or maybe in a CI pipeline. Because of that, I'm going to skip the
conformance-update (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:49:06.7003145Z verbose output in the interest of brevity.
conformance-update (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:49:06.7003403Z 
conformance-update (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:49:06.7003569Z If you would like to
conformance-update (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:49:06.7004077Z see the output, try like this:
conformance-update (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:49:06.7004332Z 
conformance-update (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:49:06.7004632Z   $ curl -L -o install-nix https://nixos.org/nix/install
conformance-update (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:49:06.7005072Z   $ sh ./install-nix
conformance-update (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:49:06.7005366Z 
conformance-update (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:49:06.7009242Z 
conformance-update (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:49:06.7010365Z ^[[32m~~> Checking for artifacts of previous installs
conformance-update (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:49:06.7017125Z ^[[0mBefore I try to install, I'll check for signs Nix already is or has
conformance-update (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:49:06.7018091Z been installed on this system.
